// core.math's IEEE leaves and bit casts at the reference values: signed
// zeros, infinities, quiet and signaling NaNs, the subnormal and normal
// edges, halves, the integers next to 2^53, 1e22, 1e300, 2^1023 and the
// greatest finite value, with sin and cos at the same huge arguments.
//
// Each wanted word is the correctly rounded binary64 result from MPFR 4.2.2:
// 53 bits, round to nearest (floor, ceil and trunc round to an integer in
// their own direction), exponent range [-1073, 1024], then mpfr_check_range
// and mpfr_subnormalize. A result is right when it lies within one unit in
// the last place of the wanted word (-0 counts one unit below +0), and a NaN
// is right where a NaN is wanted (MPFR's NaN has no payload). Each line
// prints the greatest distance its function reached. The bit casts must
// return every word unchanged, NaN payloads included.
use math: core.math

